==============================================================================================
 PART 3  RAMANUJAN <-> ZETA:  sum_N c_N(k) N^-s = sigma_{1-s}(k)/zeta(s)
==============================================================================================
  s=2.0 k= 1:  sum_N c_N(k)/N^s = 0.607927   sigma_{1-s}(k)/zeta(s) = 0.607929   match=True
  s=2.0 k= 6:  sum_N c_N(k)/N^s = 1.215852   sigma_{1-s}(k)/zeta(s) = 1.215858   match=True
  s=2.0 k=12:  sum_N c_N(k)/N^s = 1.418496   sigma_{1-s}(k)/zeta(s) = 1.418501   match=True
  s=3.0 k= 1:  sum_N c_N(k)/N^s = 0.831907   sigma_{1-s}(k)/zeta(s) = 0.831907   match=True
  s=3.0 k= 6:  sum_N c_N(k)/N^s = 1.155427   sigma_{1-s}(k)/zeta(s) = 1.155427   match=True
  s=3.0 k=12:  sum_N c_N(k)/N^s = 1.213198   sigma_{1-s}(k)/zeta(s) = 1.213198   match=True
  => the Riemann zeta function enters as the DENOMINATOR of the Ramanujan (unit-restricted) Dirichlet
     series. THM-503: L(archimedean) has NO Euler product; the UNIT-RESTRICTED atomic moments DO.

